cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the thesis below."
title: "A Window into the Future"
abstract: >-
  Predicts where in 3D a person will interact with objects next, as a 16x16x16
  voxel grid over one kitchen, from a 30-second egocentric observation window.
  A transformer encoder over per-second visual, location, 3D-object-box and gaze
  tokens, read out by a voxel-query decoder of 4096 coordinate-conditioned
  queries. Adapts FIction (CVPR 2025) to the HD-EPIC dataset.
authors:
  - family-names: "Luque Ochoa"
    given-names: "Santiago"
year: 2026
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/sluque1/Window-into-the-Future"
keywords:
  - egocentric vision
  - action anticipation
  - future interaction prediction
  - 3D scene understanding
  - HD-EPIC
preferred-citation:
